I seem to remember that something like the following proposal has already
been in this newsgroup, but here goes nevertheless. 

Polymorphing object makes the game easy, because it is possible to keep
on polymorphing the same junk object until it becomes something useful. 

Why not arrange so, that polymorphing an object repeatedly disintegrates
it.  After N polymorphs there would be a (1 - 1/N) chance that the
object disintegrates. 

Alternatively, polymorphing would have a p% chance of disintegrating
the object.  This might be a bit easier to implement, since every object
descriptor does not need to have a field counting polymorphs of the
object. 

If the junk pile beeing polymorphed gets smaller, the player would have
to replehish it. If probability of disintegration is high enough, it is
sooner or later too difficult to find new objects to add to the pile. 
